; The fur.ppx behavioural proofs (like the sift.ppx golden test next door): .mlx files compiled
; THROUGH fennec.fur.ppx and asserted on OUTPUT, not pretty-printed source. `-open Fur` mirrors
; the component/handler libs exactly (the open that lets userland write signal/get/set and `!s`).
;
;   test_fur_jsx        — the JSX-desugar sugars: bare (expr) value children (no `node`),
;                         bare (each …) (no `frag`), the `!s` read sugar — checked via Fur.to_html.
;   test_component_shape — the UNIFIED component shape (render = the trailing body, ppx-emitted
;                         `fun () ->`): proves SSR-once / render-many over Fur.Reconcile — setup
;                         runs once, render re-runs reactively, per-instance isolation, on_mount
;                         disposes on unmount. The setup-vs-render boundary, proven by behaviour.
(tests
 (names test_fur_jsx test_component_shape)
 (libraries fennec.fur fennec.fur.html fennec-hunt.unit)
 (preprocess
  (pps fennec.fur.ppx))
 (flags
  (:standard -w -a -open Fur)))
